 ### Money collection APIs
 
 | Method | Path | Purpose |
 |--------|------|---------|
 | `POST` | `/revenue/checkout` | Create a Stripe or simulated Checkout session |
+| `POST` | `/revenue/billing-portal` | Open Stripe Customer Portal (operator auth) |
 | `POST` | `/revenue/payments/:id/collect` | Complete a simulated payment (non-production) |
 | `GET` | `/revenue/earnings` | Operator earnings snapshot |
 | `POST` | `/usage/events` | Record metered usage |
 | `POST` | `/mcp` | MCP JSON-RPC tools for agents |
 
-Set `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` to a live/test Stripe key for real collection. Placeholder keys automatically use simulated checkout. Operator routes accept `Authorization: Bearer $OPERATOR_API_KEY` or a JWT signed with `JWT_SECRET`.
+Use a [restricted API key](https://docs.stripe.com/keys.md#manage-your-api-keys) (`STRIPE_RESTRICTED_KEY`, `rk_test_` / `rk_live_`) as the default. `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` is a local/test fallback; production requires `rk_live_` unless `STRIPE_ALLOW_SECRET_KEY=true` for emergency cutover. Pin API version `2026-09-30.endive` (`stripe@23`). Use a dedicated Stripe sandbox for local work and another for CI — not the account's shared test mode.
+
+Checkout Sessions omit `payment_method_types` so Dashboard dynamic payment methods apply, set `integration_identifier` (`openclaw-` + 8 letters), and fulfill **only from webhooks**. Enable these events on the webhook endpoint:
+
+- `checkout.session.completed` (fulfill only when `payment_status` is not `unpaid`)
+- `checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded` / `checkout.session.async_payment_failed`
+- `customer.subscription.created|updated|deleted`
+- `invoice.paid` / `invoice.payment_succeeded` / `invoice.payment_failed`
+- `charge.dispute.created` / `charge.refunded` / `radar.early_fraud_warning.created`
+
+Do not enable `automatic_tax` until Dashboard → Tax → Registrations shows **Collecting**. Retainer self-serve changes go through the Customer Portal, not a custom card form. Operator routes accept `Authorization: Bearer $OPERATOR_API_KEY` or a JWT signed with `JWT_SECRET`. Placeholder keys automatically use simulated checkout.
+
+### Platform controls
+
+| Area | Behavior |
+|------|----------|
+| Cryptography | Customer emails are sealed with AES-256-GCM (HKDF-SHA256 from `OPENCLAW_ENCRYPTION_KEY`). RAKs are redacted in logs. Webhook HMAC stays on Stripe's `constructEvent`. |
+| Governance | Append-only `/revenue/audit` records checkout, fulfillment, and risk actions. |
+| Observability | `/ready` reports API version, RAK, encryption, and tax-registration state. `/revenue/metrics` exposes counters. |
+| Intrusion | Sliding-window detector for signature failures, disputes, refunds, and Radar early-fraud warnings. |
+| Sales | Public `/revenue/offers` lists one-time lanes and the $8,000/mo GitOps retainer. |
+| Mesh + DAG | Paid/failed webhooks run an async DAG (`record_audit` → `emit_mesh` → `notify_ops`) and publish A2A envelopes (`source`, `target`, `intent`, `payload`, `tokens`, `trace_id`) to the in-process bus and optional `PIPEFISH_GATEWAY_URL`. |
  
